      <div type="clause" n="El. 24">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 24" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="34" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa forstele<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.24"/> oðres oxan ⁊ hine ófslea oððe bebycgge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.25"/>, selle twegen wið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.26"/> ⁊ feower<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.27"/> sceap wið anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gif he næbbe hwæt he selle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.22"/>, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.1"/> he self<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.28"/> beboht wið ðam fio.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.29"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 24" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="34" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa forstele oþres oxan ⁊ hine ofslea oððe bebycge, sylle twegen ⁊ IIII sceap wiþ anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gif he næbbe hwet he sylle, sy he self beboht wið þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> feo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 24" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa forstele oþres oxan ⁊ hine ofslea oððe bebicge, sylle twegen wið ⁊ feower sceap wyþ anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gif he nite hwæt he sylle, sy he sylf beboht wið þan feo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 24" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis furatus fuerit ouem aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.10"/> bouem et occiderit uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.11"/> uendiderit, quinque boues pro uno boue restituet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.12"/> et quatuor oues pro una oue.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 24" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="246" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hwa forstele oðres oxan ⁊ hine ofslea oððe bebycgge, selle twegen wið ⁊ feower sceap wið anum. Gif he næbbe hwæt he selle, sie he self beboht wið ðam fio.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="35" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer den Ochsen eines anderen stiehlt und ihn schlachtet oder verkauft, gebe er zwei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.1"/> dagegen und vier Schafe gegen ein [gestohlenes]. Wenn er nicht, was er hergeben könne, besitzt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.2"/>, werde er selbst [als Ersatz] für das Vieh verkauft.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone steals another’s ox and slaughters or sells it, let him give two in return, and four sheep for one [stolen]. If he does not possess what he could give, let him himself be sold [in compensation] for the livestock.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="247" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone should steal another’s ox and slay him or sell him, let him give two for it and four [sheep] for one. If he does not have what he should give, let him be sold himself in exchange for the livestock.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 22,1 and 22,4</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="35">Exodus 22.1; Exodus 22.4</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[22, 1] | [22, 4]</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><ref target="clause:Af_16">Af 16</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tæle <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tæle So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ygge, <hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> -ycge <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -ycge, sylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ygge, altered to -ycge So; -ycge, sylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oððe bebycg <hi rend="italic">folgt, durchstrichen So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oððe bebycg follows, struck through, So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fewer sceapa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fewer sceapa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylf <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylf So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">34</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fioh <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> feoh <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fioh So; feoh Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">35</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">35</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aut <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aut Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">35</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-uat <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-uat Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">35</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Aelfreds folgenden Satz bringt Quadr., wie Vulg., 7 Zeilen später</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Quadr., like Vulg., gives Aelfred’s following sentence 7 lines later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af ändert bewusst gemäss Agsä. Busse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13b); denn die in Urkk. häufige Verlesung von <hi rend="italic">U</hi> als <hi rend="italic">II</hi> war in der Zahl<hi rend="spaced">wörter</hi> schreibenden Vulgata unmöglich. In der folgenden Zeile bleibt Af der Vulgata treu. Strafgeld fehlt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af alters deliberately in accordance with A.-S. compensation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13b); for the misreading of <hi rend="italic">U</hi> as <hi rend="italic">II</hi>, frequent in charters, was impossible in the Vulgate, which writes numbers in <hi rend="italic">words</hi>. In the following line Af remains faithful to the Vulgate. A fine is lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘nicht weiss’ H</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘does not know’ H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-24.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">45</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af setzt diese Verknechtung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7b) des zur Strafzahlung Unfähigen, Agsä. Rechte gemäss, bereits zu schlichtem Diebstahl, die Exodus erst einige Zeilen später zum Einbruch. Doch blieb dem Agsachsen die Lösung durch die Sippe, <hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af, in accordance with A.-S. law, already applies this reduction to slavery (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7b) of the man unable to pay the fine to simple theft, whereas Exodus applies it only some lines later to housebreaking. The Anglo-Saxon, however, still had redemption by the kindred, <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 8</seg></note>
      </div>
